        "notes": "Frame advantage depends on the height at which it hits the opponent - the lower, the more advantaged. Tends to be -6 on block, -3 on hit against standing opponents. • Has some vertical activation range preventing it from being more than -6. Leo will always hit the opponent and land 4 frames later at the maximum. • Due to this activation range, on hit, Leo can always combo into 12F or faster specials. This is increased to 13F or faster if it is a crouching hit."
